": false,\n        \"story\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"3895034354594647645\",\n        \"shortcode\": \"DYN8RvVjo5d\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYN8RvVjo5d/\",\n        \"kind\": \"reel\",\n        \"mediaType\": \"video\",\n        \"caption\": \"Three recruiting mistakes families make while waiting for a coach to call.\\n\\nMistake 1: targeting only D1 while running no active outreach to D2 or NAIA. Coaches build boards from athletes who showed up consistently. Passive waiting is not building a relationship.\\n\\nMistake 2: generic emails. 'I'm interested in your program' goes straight to the delete folder. Specific emails with program references, real metrics, and a focused ask get responses.\\n\\nMistake 3: no follow-up system. One email is not a process. The recruiting relationship is built across multiple touches over time. No follow-up plan means disappearing from the radar.\\n\\nThe one thing that fixes all three: a plan. A real target list. Specific outreach. A consistent follow-up system. A standard for evaluating what good looks like.\\n\\nThe families who see clearly and move early make the right decision — and they do not spend more to do it.\\n\\nFind the right school — not just a school.\\nrecruitingmadesimple.app\\n\\n#RecruitingMadeSimple #CollegeRecruiting #BaseballRecruiting #SoftballRecruiting #TravelBaseball #TravelSoftball #FitScore #StudentAthlete #CollegeBound #RecruitingTips #HighSchoolBaseball #HighSchoolSoftball #D1Baseball #D2Baseball #NAIABaseball #RecruitingProcess\",\n        \"altText\": null,\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-12T00:06:10.000Z\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"id\": \"78364825795\",\n          \"handle\": \"recruiting_made_simple\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Recruiting Made Simple\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://scontent-lax3-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-19/653660691_17863425873609796_7107605746059487773_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e0_s150x150_tt6&_nc_cat=107&ig_cache