ial"},"coauthors":[],"taggedUsers":[],"location":null,"isPaidPartnership":false,"sponsors":[],"commentsDisabled":false,"isPinned":false,"story":null},{"id":"3895034354594647645","shortcode":"DYN8RvVjo5d","url":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYN8RvVjo5d/","kind":"reel","mediaType":"video","caption":"Three recruiting mistakes families make while waiting for a coach to call.\n\nMistake 1: targeting only D1 while running no active outreach to D2 or NAIA. Coaches build boards from athletes who showed up consistently. Passive waiting is not building a relationship.\n\nMistake 2: generic emails. 'I'm interested in your program' goes straight to the delete folder. Specific emails with program references, real metrics, and a focused ask get responses.\n\nMistake 3: no follow-up system. One email is not a process. The recruiting relationship is built across multiple touches over time. No follow-up plan means disappearing from the radar.\n\nThe one thing that fixes all three: a plan. A real target list. Specific outreach. A consistent follow-up system. A standard for evaluating what good looks like.\n\nThe families who see clearly and move early make the right decision — and they do not spend more to do it.\n\nFind the right school — not just a school.\nrecruitingmadesimple.app\n\n#RecruitingMadeSimple #CollegeRecruiting #BaseballRecruiting #SoftballRecruiting #TravelBaseball #TravelSoftball #FitScore #StudentAthlete #CollegeBound #RecruitingTips #HighSchoolBaseball #HighSchoolSoftball #D1Baseball #D2Baseball #NAIABaseball #RecruitingProcess","altText":null,"createdAt":"2026-05-12T00:06:10.000Z","owner":{"id":"78364825795","handle":"recruiting_made_simple","displayName":"Recruiting Made Simple","avatarUrl":"https://scontent-lax3-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-19/653660691_17863425873609796_7107605746059487773_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e0_s150x150_tt6&_nc_cat=107&ig_cache_key=GBMS9iZEBKvxsHY-AB2qZrHESaNibmNDAQAB1501500j-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=669407&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6InByb2ZpbGV